THE LIVE CAPTURE AT THE R-I HALT, BASED AT THE BRANCH TIP.

WHY THIS EXISTS ALONGSIDE L6_pass4_exit_state.diff
  L6_pass4_exit_state.diff was generated BEFORE the halt filing was committed, so it carries 20
  sections — the 19 product files PLUS the harness re-pin, which was still uncommitted at that
  moment. It remains exact and is sealed as the record of that state; it applies at ITS OWN base
  (dfcdc9e), where the harness re-pin had not yet landed.
  Committing the halt filing moved the harness re-pin into history, so at the tip the live
  uncommitted delta is 19 sections, not 20. A successor reconstructing from the TIP needs a capture
  based AT the tip — otherwise they must first check out an ancestor, which is the kind of quiet
  step that gets skipped. This file is that capture. Nothing about the tree changed between the two;
  only the base did.

